"# SPEC 136 — McFrontend Handbook

**Status:** GENERATED

> **Role: generated handbook.** Authority: Spec 135 FE rows (policy register) + Spec 126 (contract) and Spec 127 (procedure); this spec is GENERATED from surface-rule-map.json — do not hand-edit. It is the reading surface of the McFrontend pair (Spec 124 R-GV). If this page and a register row disagree, the register row governs on policy and Spec 126 or Spec 127 on the contract and the procedure; fix the register or the generator, never this page. A new ruling is a new row in Spec 135, never a line here.
>
> **Citation form.** `Spec 136 §<line id> (FE-nn)`, e.g. `Spec 136 §fe.01 (FE-01)`. The line id is the bold id that starts each line (fe.<n> for a Spec 135 FE-row); the rule id is the register row it summarises.

<!-- GENERATED by `node scripts/surfaces/generate-surface-handbook.mjs --write`. Do not edit by hand: `--check` and `src/tests/surfaces/handbook-rule-map.logic.test.ts` fail on a stale file. -->

v1 covers the 3 FE rulings of Spec 135. The policy rows R-01..R-34 are in Spec 128 §5 until MF-31.

**\"Comply with Spec 136\"** means: for McFrontend work, read the lines that cover what you touch, then follow the register row each cites. Every line cites its binding rule id; the row in `docs/specs/02-web-admin/135_mcfrontend_decisions_register.md` is the authority, with its reasons, evidence and dated notes.

## 1. Standard and policy pairs

| Role | Spec | Path |
|---|---|---|
| Contract (what is built) | Spec 126 | `docs/specs/02-web-admin/126_maxbld_surface_standard.md` |
| Procedure (how it is converted) | Spec 127 | `docs/specs/02-web-admin/127_surface_conversion_procedure.md` |
| Policy (what is ruled) | Spec 128 | `docs/specs/02-web-admin/128_surface_standard_policy.md` |
| Register (the FE rulings) | Spec 135 | `docs/specs/02-web-admin/135_mcfrontend_decisions_register.md` |

On a policy question the register governs (Spec 128 §5 dated note 2026-11-04; Spec 124 R-GV).

**What is generated.** Everything below, from the Spec 135 register table by `scripts/surfaces/generate-surface-handbook.mjs` (status and lock paths read by `scripts/analysis/mcbylaws/cite-parse.mjs` `parseRegisterRows`, the reader gate arm C uses). The rule map `scripts/surfaces/_schema/surface-rule-map.json` is generated from the same rows, not hand-written; `src/tests/surfaces/handbook-rule-map.logic.test.ts` (FE-10) locks that every register row has exactly one line and every line cites exactly one row.

**Rules rendered: 3**: 3 in force (1 OWED, whose lock is still to land), 0 history. Each line: its line id, the reading headline, the register status, the lock that enforces it (RULED rows only; an OWED row shows the lock it owes) and the number of dated notes under the row.

**Contents.** 1 Standard and policy pairs · 2 Rules · 3 History

## 2. Rules

- **fe.01** Ruling for FE-01, a plain sentence.
  Status: RULED 2026-11-04

- **fe.02** Ruling for FE-02, a plain sentence.
  Status: RULED 2026-11-09 · Enforced by: src/tests/surfaces/x.logic.test.ts · +2 dated notes

- **fe.03** Ruling for FE-03, a plain sentence.
  Status: OWED · lock owed: src/tests/surfaces/y.logic.test.ts · +2 dated notes

## 3. History

Rows retired or struck. Listed only so old citations resolve. Nothing here is a rule you must follow.

None yet.

## Operating Boundaries

### Target Files
- `scripts/surfaces/generate-surface-handbook.mjs` (the generator; `--write` / `--check`)
- `scripts/analysis/gates/rule-map.mjs` (the handbook registry keyed by spec id and the shared CLI shell)
- `scripts/analysis/mcbylaws/cite-parse.mjs` (the one reader of a row's status and lock paths)
- `scripts/surfaces/_schema/surface-rule-map.json` (the generated rule map)
- `src/tests/surfaces/handbook-rule-map.logic.test.ts` (the lock)
"

